<title>USA: Puget Sound president resigns after merger.</title>
<headline>Puget Sound president resigns after merger.</headline>
<dateline>BELLEVUE, Wash. 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Puget Sound Energy said its president and chief operating officer William Vititoe had resigned but would continue to serve as a special consultant on industry issues.</p>
<p>The resignation came less than a week after the company was formed by the merger of Puget Sound Power &amp; Light Co and Washington Energy Co. Vititoe had served as chairman and chief executive of Washington Energy.</p>
<p>At a weekend meeting, the Puget Sound Energy board elected Richard Sonstelie chairman and chief executive officer, William Weaver vice chairman and chairman of unregulated subsidiaries and James Torgerson as chief financial officer.</p>
<p>-- Seattle bureau 206-386-4848</p>
